  "description": "NPC dialogue from a small local language model, through LLamaSharp: one model loaded per process and run on a queue of its own, each conversation kept read so a turn reads only its own line, personas and per-turn facts, replies limited by a grammar to a line, a mood and an action the game allows, streamed a checked sentence at a time, with player input cleaned and an authored line to fall back on. Runs on the CPU by default; bring the LLamaSharp backend you ship (Cpu, Vulkan or Cuda). No engine dependency.",
